BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//wmutschl//scripts calendar//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
METHOD:PUBLISH
X-WR-CALNAME:Backups and maintenance
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:monthly-checks@scripts.mutschler.dev
DTSTAMP:20261120T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261212
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261213
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYDAY=2SA
SUMMARY:Backups: monthly checks (Wyse\, Mac mini\, Macs)
DESCRIPTION:healthchecks.io reports failed and missed jobs by itself\; this
  is the look around.\n- healthchecks.io: open the dashboard\, every check 
 green.\n- Wyse: run the commands in section 10.4 (disk usage\, device stat
 s\, btrbk list latest\, timers\, journals of send/scrub/offsite\, /srv/ha-
 backups\, docker system df\, compare installed files with ~/scripts\, syst
 emctl --failed).\n- Wyse: reboot only if /var/run/reboot-required exists\,
  through dell-wyse-reboot-check (section 11.3).\n- Mac mini: the commands 
 in section 10.7 of the Mac mini guide\; Gitea's System Notices and Actions
  → Runners.\n- Every Mac\, including the MacBook Air: Time Machine's lat
 est backup is recent (tmutil latestbackup).\n- MacBook Pro: the office dis
 k has a backup from the last weeks.\nWyse guide 10.4: https://mutschler.de
 v/linux/wyse-ubuntu-nextcloud-aio/#104-regular-checks\nMac mini guide 10.7
 : https://mutschler.dev/apple/mac-mini-gitea-modcraft/#107-regular-checks\
 nBackup strategy: https://mutschler.dev/stuff/backup/
URL:https://mutschler.dev/linux/wyse-ubuntu-nextcloud-aio/#104-regular-chec
 ks
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Backups
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Backups: monthly checks (Wyse\, Mac mini\, Macs)
TRIGGER:PT9H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quarterly-drills-wyse-ha@scripts.mutschler.dev
DTSTAMP:20261120T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=3;BYDAY=1SA
SUMMARY:Restore drill: Wyse and Home Assistant (quarterly)
DESCRIPTION:A backup counts only once a restore from it has worked.\n- Copy
  one file back from the newest hourly snapshot and the same file from HDD 
 1. Pass: both match the original (sha256sum).\n- AIO's backup section: Che
 ck backup integrity. Pass: AIO reports the repository as intact.\n- Extrac
 t one file from the newest Borg archive on the Wyse\, without AIO\, outsid
 e the nightly jobs. Pass: the file opens\, so the Borg password in the pas
 sword manager works.\n- Home Assistant\, Settings → System → Backups. 
 Pass: the newest backup is on dell_wyse\, and the emergency kit is in the 
 password manager.\nWyse guide 10.5: https://mutschler.dev/linux/wyse-ubunt
 u-nextcloud-aio/#105-restore-drills
URL:https://mutschler.dev/linux/wyse-ubuntu-nextcloud-aio/#105-restore-dril
 ls
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Backups
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Restore drill: Wyse and Home Assistant (quarterly)
TRIGGER:PT9H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quarterly-drills-gitea@scripts.mutschler.dev
DTSTAMP:20261120T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261219
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261220
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=3;BYDAY=3SA
SUMMARY:Restore drill: Gitea on the MacBook (quarterly)
DESCRIPTION:- Restore the newest Gitea backup on the MacBook\, with the ove
 rride that turns mirroring off\, then remove the drill there. Pass: Gitea 
 is healthy and lists every repository.\n- Gitea's Site Administration → 
 System Notices. Pass: no mirror keeps failing.\n- Add mirrors for new repo
 sitories on GitHub\, GitLab and Dynare's GitLab.\nMac mini guide 10.4: htt
 ps://mutschler.dev/apple/mac-mini-gitea-modcraft/#104-restore-drills
URL:https://mutschler.dev/apple/mac-mini-gitea-modcraft/#104-restore-drills
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Backups
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Restore drill: Gitea on the MacBook (quarterly)
TRIGGER:PT9H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quarterly-updates@scripts.mutschler.dev
DTSTAMP:20261120T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261226
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261227
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;INTERVAL=3;BYDAY=-1SA
SUMMARY:Updates: sidecars\, Gitea\, OrbStack (quarterly)
DESCRIPTION:- Wyse: pull and restart the Tailscale sidecar (section 10.6)\;
  a reviewed apt full-upgrade for the Docker packages in a maintenance wind
 ow.\n- Mac mini: Gitea and the Gitea runner (release notes first\; run the
  backup before changing the image tag)\, PostgreSQL minor versions\, both 
 Tailscale sidecars\, OrbStack (section 10.6).\n- After git pull in ~/scrip
 ts on either machine: follow the README's "After a change".\nWyse guide 10
 .6: https://mutschler.dev/linux/wyse-ubuntu-nextcloud-aio/#106-updates\nMa
 c mini guide 10.6: https://mutschler.dev/apple/mac-mini-gitea-modcraft/#10
 6-updates
URL:https://mutschler.dev/linux/wyse-ubuntu-nextcloud-aio/#106-updates
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Backups
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Updates: sidecars\, Gitea\, OrbStack (quarterly)
TRIGGER:PT9H
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yearly-drills-wyse-ha@scripts.mutschler.dev
DTSTAMP:20261120T120000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270102
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270103
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=1;BYDAY=1SA
SUMMARY:Restore drill: Wyse and Home Assistant (yearly)
DESCRIPTION:- Restore a Home Assistant backup from /srv/ha-backups onto a s
 pare SD card/SSD or into a VM\, through Restore from backup in HA's onboar
 ding\, with the emergency kit. Pass: HA starts with my configuration.\n- C
 ompare the Storage Box mirror with HDD 2 right after a nightly run (takes 
 hours)\, and look at the snapshot list in the Hetzner Console. Pass: no di
 fferences\; 10 daily snapshots are there.\n- Test HDD 1's LUKS passphrase 
 from the password manager\, and check that the initrd still has my SSH key
 . Pass: the passphrase is accepted\; my key is listed.\n- Go through the r
 ecovery material (Wyse guide 10.2). Pass: every password and file is there
  and works.\n- Check dracut-sshd's releases (section 10.6).\nWyse guide 10
 .5: https://mutschler.dev/linux/wyse-ubuntu-nextcloud-aio/#105-restore-dri
 lls\nHome Assistant restore: https://mutschler.dev/linux/raspi-home-assist
 ant-os/#step-8-restore-from-a-backup
URL:https://mutschler.dev/linux/wyse-ubuntu-nextcloud-aio/#105-restore-dril
 ls
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:Backups
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Restore drill: Wyse and Home Assistant (yearly)
